    overview: "Bipolar disorder involves episodes of mania or hypomania and depression, while substances and withdrawal can mimic or worsen changes in mood, sleep, energy, judgment, and behavior. Diagnosis requires a careful timeline across days and weeks, previous episodes, family history, medicines, and periods of reduced use.",
