    overview: "Eating disorders are serious illnesses involving disturbances in eating behavior and related thoughts or emotions, and they can co-occur with substance use disorders. Alcohol, stimulants, laxatives, cannabis, sedatives, and other substances may be connected to appetite, weight, emotion regulation, or compensatory behavior.",
