    overview: "Obsessive-compulsive disorder involves intrusive, unwanted obsessions and repetitive compulsions that consume time or cause distress and impairment. A person may use substances to reduce anxiety temporarily, while intoxication or withdrawal can worsen intrusive thoughts, checking, sleep, or the ability to resist rituals.",
    evidence: "Exposure and response prevention, a form of cognitive behavioral therapy, is a well-established treatment for OCD, and medication may also be used. When a substance use disorder is present, integrated planning should address both conditions and coordinate exposure work with withdrawal, medication, and relapse risks.",
